{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.121.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-35669-http",
              "name": "StockMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-35669 medium vulnerability for http package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "http before 0.13.3 vulnerable to header injection"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4rgh-jx4f-qfcq",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-35669\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: http\nVersion: 0.13.2\nFix Version: 0.13.3\nType: dart-pub\nLocation: /pubspec.lock\nData Namespace: github:language:dart\nLink: [CVE-2020-35669](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4rgh-jx4f-qfcq)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2020-35669**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | http  | 0.13.2  | 0.13.3  | dart-pub  | /pubspec.lock  | github:language:dart  | [CVE-2020-35669](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4rgh-jx4f-qfcq)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:pub/http@0.13.2?hosted_url=pub.dev"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-3095-Flutter",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-3095 critical vulnerability for Flutter package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The implementation of backslash parsing in the Dart URI class for versions prior to 2.18 and Flutter versions prior to 3.30 differs from the WhatWG URL standards. Dart uses the RFC 3986 syntax, which creates incompatibilities with the '\\' characters in URIs, which can lead to auth bypass in webapps interpreting URIs. We recommend updating Dart or Flutter to mitigate the issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-3095",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-3095\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: Flutter\nVersion: 1.0.0\nFix Version: 3.3.3\nType: pod\nLocation: /ios/Podfile.lock\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2022-3095](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-3095)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-3095**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | Flutter  | 1.0.0  | 3.3.3  | pod  | /ios/Podfile.lock  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2022-3095](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-3095)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:cocoapods/Flutter@1.0.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-36826-sentry",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-36826 medium vulnerability for sentry package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sentry is an error tracking and performance monitoring platform. Starting in version 8.21.0 and prior to version 23.5.2, an authenticated user can download a debug or artifact bundle from arbitrary organizations and projects with a known bundle ID. The user does not need to be a member of the organization or have permissions on the project. A patch was issued in version 23.5.2 to ensure authorization checks are properly scoped on requests to retrieve debug or artifact bundles. Authenticated users who do not have the necessary permissions on the particular project are no longer able to download them. Sentry SaaS users do not need to take any action. Self-Hosted Sentry users should upgrade to version 23.5.2 or higher."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-36826",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-36826\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: sentry\nVersion: 9.6.0\nFix Version: 23.5.2\nType: dart-pub\nLocation: /pubspec.lock\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-36826](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-36826)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-36826**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | sentry  | 9.6.0  | 23.5.2  | dart-pub  | /pubspec.lock  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-36826](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-36826)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:pub/sentry@9.6.0?hosted_url=pub.dev"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27704-Flutter",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-27704 high vulnerability for Flutter package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Dart and Flutter SDKs provide software development kits for the Dart programming language. In versions of the Dart SDK prior to 3.11.0 and the Flutter SDK prior to version 3.41.0, when the pub client (`dart pub` and `flutter pub`) extracts a package in the pub cache, a malicious package archive can have files extracted outside the destination directory in the `PUB_CACHE`.  A fix has been landed in commit 26c6985c742593d081f8b58450f463a584a4203a. By normalizing the file path before writing file, the attacker can no longer traverse up via a symlink. This patch is released in Dart 3.11.0 and Flutter 3.41.0.vAll packages on pub.dev have been vetted for this vulnerability. New packages are no longer allowed to contain symlinks. The pub client itself doesn't upload symlinks, but duplicates the linked entry, and has been doing this for years. Those whose dependencies are all from pub.dev, third-party repositories trusted to not contain malicious code, or git dependencies are not affected by this vulnerability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27704",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27704\nSeverity: high\nPackage: Flutter\nVersion: 1.0.0\nFix Version: 3.41.0\nType: pod\nLocation: /ios/Podfile.lock\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-27704](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27704)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27704**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | Flutter  | 1.0.0  | 3.41.0  | pod  | /ios/Podfile.lock  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-27704](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27704)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:cocoapods/Flutter@1.0.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24829-sentry",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24829 medium vulnerability for sentry package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sentry is an error tracking and performance monitoring platform. Sentry’s integration platform provides a way for external services to interact with Sentry. One of such integrations, the Phabricator integration (maintained by Sentry) with version \u003c=24.1.1 contains a constrained SSRF vulnerability. An attacker could make Sentry send POST HTTP requests to arbitrary URLs (including internal IP addresses) by providing an unsanitized input to the Phabricator integration. However, the body payload is constrained to a specific format. If an attacker has access to a Sentry instance, this allows them to: 1. interact with internal network; 2. scan local/remote ports. This issue has been fixed in Sentry self-hosted release 24.1.2, and has already been mitigated on sentry.io on February 8. Users are advised to upgrade. There are no known workarounds for this vulnerability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24829",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24829\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: sentry\nVersion: 9.6.0\nFix Version: 24.1.2\nType: dart-pub\nLocation: /pubspec.lock\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-24829](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24829)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-24829**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | sentry  | 9.6.0  | 24.1.2  | dart-pub  | /pubspec.lock  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-24829](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24829)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:pub/sentry@9.6.0?hosted_url=pub.dev"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
